That's the before and after the fix. Just needed to obtain logical size outside of `access` construction. That's because of the interaction of these two methods, and the fact that access() takes a shared lock until destruct.

```size_t map::size() const NOEXCEPT
{
    std::shared_lock field_lock(field_mutex_);
    return logical_;
}

size_t map::allocate(size_t chunk) NOEXCEPT
{
    std::unique_lock field_lock(field_mutex_);
    if (!loaded_ || is_add_overflow(logical_, chunk))
        return storage::eof;

    auto end = logical_ + chunk;
    if (end > capacity_)
    {
        const auto size = to_capacity(end);
        std::unique_lock remap_lock(remap_mutex_);
        if (!remap_(size))
            return storage::eof;
    }

    std::swap(logical_, end);
    return end;
}```
